@startuml
title Installed GSLT lookahead reuses the existing speculative search
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #102027
  RoundCorner 16
}

rectangle "Rholang application\ninline Theory/Module and FLT send" as app #DCEEFF
rectangle "F1R3Lang checked lowering\nP[n] or P[*] request" as lower #BBDEFB
rectangle "Lookahead request server\ninstalled handle and host budget" as server #B2DFDB
rectangle "Existing breadth-first Explorer\nEveryTrace frontier" as search #D1C4E9
rectangle "RSpace enabled COMM edges" as rho #E1BEE7
rectangle "Checked GSLT one-step roster\nsemantic transition kernel" as guest #E1BEE7
rectangle "Success / failure / truncated\ntrace-indexed PathMaps" as maps #FFF9C4
rectangle "Rholang receive and query\nauthorized observation" as receive #C8E6C9
rectangle "Typed refusal\nno partial publication" as refusal #FFCDD2

app --> lower
lower --> server
server --> search : checked request
server --> refusal : missing authority or budget
search --> rho : enumerate and fire
search --> guest : enumerate and fire
rho --> search : exact successor state
guest --> search : term and receipt
search --> maps : complete branch evidence
maps --> receive : approved reply wire

note bottom of guest
  Rule and proof occurrences remain distinct.
  Whole normalization is not one lookahead step.
end note
@enduml
